{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "package": "vim",
  "installation_title": "Installation of Vim",
  "contents_title": "Contents of Vim",
  "installed_labels": {
    "programs": "Installed programs",
    "directories": "Installed directory"
  },
  "installation_blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First, change the default location of the"
        },
        {
          "type": "filename",
          "text": "vimrc"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "configuration file to"
        },
        {
          "type": "filename",
          "text": "/etc"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ":"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Prepare Vim for compilation:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Compile the package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "To prepare the tests, ensure that user"
        },
        {
          "type": "systemitem",
          "text": "tester"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "can write to the source tree and exclude one file containing tests requiring"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "curl"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "or"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "wget"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ":"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now run the tests as user"
        },
        {
          "type": "systemitem",
          "text": "tester"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ":"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The test suite outputs a lot of binary data to the screen. This can cause issues with the settings of the current terminal (especially while we are overriding the"
        },
        {
          "type": "envar",
          "text": "TERM"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "variable to satisfy some assumptions of the test suite). The problem can be avoided by redirecting the output to a log file as shown above. A successful test will show"
        },
        {
          "type": "computeroutput",
          "text": "FAILED: 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "in the log file at completion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two tests, Test_client_server_stopinsert() and Test_popup_setbuf(), are known to fail on some systems."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Install the package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Many users reflexively type"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "vi"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "instead of"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "vim"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". To allow execution of"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "vim"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "when users habitually enter"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "vi"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", create a symlink for both the binary and the man page in the provided languages:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "By default, Vim's documentation is installed in"
        },
        {
          "type": "filename",
          "text": "/usr/share/vim"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The following symlink allows the documentation to be accessed via"
        },
        {
          "type": "filename",
          "text": "/usr/share/doc/vim-9.2.1025"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", making it consistent with the location of documentation for other packages:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 7
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If an X Window System is going to be installed on the LFS system, it may be necessary to recompile Vim after installing X. Vim comes with a GUI version of the editor that requires X and some additional libraries to be installed. For more information on this process, refer to the Vim documentation and the Vim installation page in the BLFS book at"
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/view/13.1-systemd/postlfs/vim.html",
          "label": "https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/view/13.1-systemd/postlfs/vim.html"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "installed_term_kinds": {
    "ex": "program",
    "rview": "program",
    "rvim": "program",
    "vi": "program",
    "view": "program",
    "vim": "program",
    "vimdiff": "program",
    "vimtutor": "program",
    "xxd": "program"
  }
}
